1:const mutationQueues = new Map();
2:
3:export function queueStorageMutation(key, operation) {
4:  const previous = mutationQueues.get(key) ?? Promise.resolve();
5:  const queued = previous.catch(() => {}).then(operation);
6:
7:  mutationQueues.set(key, queued);
8:  queued.then(
9:    () => {
10:      if (mutationQueues.get(key) === queued) mutationQueues.delete(key);
11:    },
12:    () => {
13:      if (mutationQueues.get(key) === queued) mutationQueues.delete(key);
14:    },
15:  );
16:
17:  return queued;
18:}
19:
20:export function mutateStorageValue(key, fallback, mutate) {
21:  return queueStorageMutation(key, async () => {
22:    const result = await chrome.storage.local.get(key);
23:    const value = result[key] ?? structuredClone(fallback);
24:    const nextValue = (await mutate(value)) ?? value;
25:    await chrome.storage.local.set({ [key]: nextValue });
26:    return nextValue;
27:  });
28:}
--- STORE_LISTING.md:115-210 ---
115:
116:Meridian processes the following **entirely on your device** to provide its
117:features:
118:
119:- **Browsing activity** â€” open tab titles, URLs, domains, tab-group membership,
120:  and tab activation/order, used to display, search, and manage your tabs. A
121:  local search index and workspace/UI state are stored in `chrome.storage.local`.
122:- **Website content** â€” after a page loads, Meridian reads its meta description
123:  and H1/H2 headings so local search can match page context beyond the title and
124:  URL. It does not read form input or other page-body text.
125:- **Screenshots** â€” Meridian captures the visible area of active tabs (and,
126:  during a user-requested full refresh, cycles eligible tabs) to render thumbnail
127:  cards and previews. Screenshots are stored as JPEG data in
128:  `chrome.storage.local`, capped at 200 entries / ~50 MB, and a tab's thumbnail
129:  is removed when the tab closes.
130:- **Local & sync storage** â€” preferences (theme, background, search provider,
131:  enabled local-search sources, new-tab behavior, optional homepage, domain
132:  grouping) are stored in `chrome.storage.sync` and may sync through your own
133:  Chrome profile. Workspaces, search metadata, thumbnails, the Meridian/previous
134:  tab IDs, and an uploaded custom background image stay in `chrome.storage.local`
135:  / IndexedDB and are not synced.
136:- **Optional bookmarks & history** â€” off by default. Meridian requests bookmark
137:  or history access only when you enable that source in Settings â†’ Local Search
138:  or select its search scope, and queries it only to show local-search results.
139:  It keeps no separate persistent copy; revoking access turns the source off.
140:- **External requests** â€” search-provider icons load from fixed Google,
141:  DuckDuckGo, Bing, and Brave icon URLs (these contain no visited URL); favicons
142:  resolve through Chrome's packaged `_favicon` provider (not Google S2); the
143:  background settings load photo previews and selected photos from
144:  `picsum.photos` by seed. Starting a web search, opening a result, or choosing a
145:  custom homepage navigates your browser to that destination normally.
146:- **Retention & deletion** â€” data persists in local/sync storage until replaced,
147:  evicted, cleared, or removed with the extension or profile. Closing a tab
148:  deletes its cached thumbnail and search entry (including extracted metadata).
149:  You can clear all extension data through Chrome's controls.
150:- **No telemetry or backend** â€” Meridian has no Meridian-operated server, no
151:  analytics or advertising SDK, no account system, and no telemetry uploader.
152:
153:---
154:
155:## 4. Permission justifications
156:
157:Paste each string into the matching "why do you need this permission?" field.
158:
159:### Required permissions
160:
161:**`tabs`**
162:Read tab titles, URLs, domains, and group/window membership and act on tabs
163:(activate, close, move, group, restore) so Meridian can render the new-tab page's
164:tab cards, power local tab search, and manage tabs from its UI.
165:
166:**`tabGroups`**
167:Read and manage Chrome tab groups so Meridian's workspace lanes reflect and can
168:modify tab-group membership and grouping.
169:
170:**`storage`**
171:Persist the user's preferences, workspaces, tab-search index (including extracted
172:page metadata), thumbnail cache, and tab-tracking state in
173:`chrome.storage.local`/`chrome.storage.sync` so settings and layout survive
174:across sessions.
175:
176:**`unlimitedStorage`**
177:Screenshot thumbnails are stored as JPEG data URLs and can exceed the default
178:storage quota. `unlimitedStorage` lets the local thumbnail cache hold enough
179:entries to be useful; usage is still bounded in code to 200 entries / ~50 MB with
180:LRU eviction.
181:
182:**`favicon`**
183:Display site icons for tabs and search results by resolving page URLs through
184:Chrome's packaged `_favicon` provider, avoiding third-party favicon lookups.
185:
186:**`sidePanel`**
187:Provide Meridian's side-panel UI, which opens when the toolbar icon is clicked.
188:
189:**`scripting`**
190:After an open tab finishes loading, run a one-shot extractor that reads only that
191:page's meta description and H1/H2 heading text into the local tab-search index,
192:so local search can match page context beyond the title and URL. It does not read
193:form input or other page-body content. `scripting` (rather than click-scoped
194:`activeTab`) is required because this indexing happens automatically on page
195:load, not from a user click.
196:
197:**`host_permissions: <all_urls>`**
198:Allow two automatic, non-click actions across the tabs the user already has open:
199:(1) capturing the visible tab via `captureVisibleTab` after tab activation, after
200:a page finishes loading, and during a user-requested full refresh, to build
201:thumbnail cards; and (2) running the load-time meta/H1/H2 metadata extractor
202:above. Chrome's click-scoped `activeTab` cannot authorize these automatic
203:background actions, so broad host access is required for the shipped
204:live-thumbnail and auto-indexing behavior. Meridian skips Chrome-internal and
205:other privileged pages and makes no network request to a Meridian server.
206:
207:### Optional permissions (requested only on demand)
208:
209:**`bookmarks`** *(optional)*
210:Requested only when the user enables bookmark search in Settings â†’ Local Search
